# The Google Picker (docs.google.com) validates the API key's website restriction against the
# Referer it receives; with `Referrer-Policy: same-origin` it gets none and fails with
# "The API developer key is invalid". The zone's "Add security headers" Managed Transform stamps
# `same-origin` after Pages, so this rule alone does not win on deployed hosts: the effective
# override is the zone rule in infrastructure/multi-cloud/terraform/cloudflare/embed-framing.tf.
# Kept here so the intent also holds for self-hosted/Pages-only deployments.
/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Overwritten at deploy time with environment values; must never be served stale.
/config.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
